<title>USA: US FTC ends probe of Dana buy of Clark-Hurth.</title>
<headline>US FTC ends probe of Dana buy of Clark-Hurth.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Trade Commission said Friday it had granted early termination of its investigation of Dana Corp's acquisition of Ingersoll-Rand Co unit Clark-Hurth.</p>
<p>The move effectively clears the way for the purchase of the off-highway vehicle parts maker, announced Dec 20, which Dana at the time said was the biggest acquisition in its 92-year history, without giving terms or conditions.</p>
<p>Clark-Hurth's 1995 sales were about $350 million, Dana said.</p>
</text>
